# Maswada AI integration contract

Ahmad is the frontend developer. Treat `backend/src/routes/ai.ts` as the only backend surface the frontend needs for AI. Do not walk him through OpenAI, services, or validators unless he asks. The route file is the menu of HTTP calls.

Mounted in `backend/src/app.ts` at `/api/ai`. Every route requires Clerk auth, same pattern as notes in `frontend/src/hooks/useApiNotes.tsx`: `Authorization: Bearer ${token}` from `useAuth().getToken()`, `POST`, `Content-Type: application/json`, base URL `VITE_API_URL` or `http://localhost:3001`.

## Endpoints

All three return `{ result: string }`. They do not save the note. The UI decides whether to replace the editor text.

- `POST /api/ai/summarize`
  - Body: `{ noteId?: uuid } | { text: string }`
  - One of `noteId` or `text` is required.
- `POST /api/ai/rewrite`
  - Body: `{ mode: "comedy" | "formal" | "casual" }` plus `noteId` or `text`.
  - `mode` is required.
- `POST /api/ai/translate`
  - Body: `{ noteId?: uuid } | { text: string }`
  - English becomes Arabic, Arabic becomes English. No target-language field.

Prefer `noteId` when the note is already saved, so the backend reads stored content. Send `text` for unsaved editor content.

## Errors the UI should handle

- `400` `{ error: "Validation failed", details: [{ path, message }] }` when the body is missing `noteId`/`text`, or rewrite is missing `mode`.
- `401` when the Clerk token is missing.
- `500` `{ error: "Internal server error" }` for OpenAI or other failures.

Show a loading state. These calls are slow.
